  "question": {
    "text": "If the tangent at a point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></math> on the parabola <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></math> is parallel to the line <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp;and the tangents at the points <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math> on the ellipse <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>1</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp;are perpendicular to the line <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math>, then the area of the triangle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi><mi>R</mi></math> is:"
  },
